# AAS: ASCII adjust AL after subtraction (Intel SDM pseudocode for the
# 286 and later). When AL's low nibble is above 9 or AF is set:
# AX = AX - 106h (AL - 6 with its borrow, then AH - 1) and AF = CF = 1; otherwise AF = CF = 0. Then AL keeps only its low
# nibble. OF, SF, ZF and PF are undefined. Bound to AX by the decoder.
read ax dst 16
read_flag old_af AF
trunc al ax 8
const low_mask 8 15
and low al low_mask
const nine 8 9
ult big nine low
or adjust big old_af
const step 16 262
const none 16 0
select amount adjust step none
sub adjusted ax amount
const keep 16 65295
and result adjusted keep
write dst result
flag AF adjust
flag CF adjust
undef_flag OF
undef_flag SF
undef_flag ZF
undef_flag PF
retire
